- entry .WorkingDirectory   the directory a program was launched in, as a contextual value
+ entry .WorkingDirectory   la directory in cui è stato lanciato un programma, come valore contestuale

= entry .WorkingDirectory   the directory a program was launched in, as a contextual value
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `WorkingDirectory` names one directory, as `#directory()` text; a method which
-       resolves a relative path against the working directory takes one as a `using`
-       parameter, rather than reading `user.dir` from a global. The ones to import by name are
-       in the `workingDirectories` package: `javaBaseWorkingDirectory` is the JVM's `user.dir`,
-       `systemWorkingDirectory` reads `user.dir` from the `System` in scope,
-       `wasiWorkingDirectory` a Wasm component's initial directory, and
-       `daemonClientWorkingDirectory` (from `ethereal`) the directory each invocation of a
-       daemon was made from. `WorkingDirectory(path)` makes one from any path value, and the
-       top-level `workingDirectory[Path on Linux]` resolves the one in scope to a path type.
+       Un `WorkingDirectory` nomina una directory, come testo `#directory()`; un metodo che
+       risolve un percorso relativo rispetto alla directory di lavoro ne prende uno come parametro
+       `using`, anziché leggere `user.dir` da un globale. Quelli da importare per nome sono nel
+       package `workingDirectories`: `javaBaseWorkingDirectory` è lo `user.dir` della JVM,
+       `systemWorkingDirectory` legge `user.dir` dal `System` nell'ambito,
+       `wasiWorkingDirectory` la directory iniziale di un componente Wasm, e
+       `daemonClientWorkingDirectory` (da `ethereal`) la directory da cui è stata fatta ciascuna
+       invocazione di un demone. `WorkingDirectory(path)` ne crea uno da qualsiasi valore di
+       percorso, e il `workingDirectory[Path on Linux]` di primo livello risolve quello
+       nell'ambito in un tipo di percorso.

=       top-level `workingDirectory[Path on Linux]` resolves the one in scope to a path type.
